# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "How to tune the configuration options for the latest version of Shaded lightcones"
msgstr "Cara menyelaraskan pilihan konfigurasi untuk versi terkini Shaded lightcones"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "How to tune the configuration options"
msgstr "Cara menyelaraskan pilihan konfigurasi"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"addons/qiskit-addon-slc/guides/configuration-options.ipynb\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The bounds computation is exact in principle but approximate in practice: evolving a Pauli error\n"
"term through a circuit produces an operator with exponentially many terms, and finding the spectral\n"
"norm of the resulting commutator is itself expensive. The options below control that cost. They fall\n"
"into three groups:\n"
msgstr ""
"Pengiraan sempadan adalah tepat pada prinsipnya tetapi hampiran dalam amalan: mengembangkan satu sebutan ralat Pauli\n"
"melalui litar menghasilkan operator dengan sebutan yang banyak secara eksponen, dan mencari norma\n"
"spektrum bagi komutator yang terhasil itu sendiri adalah mahal. Pilihan di bawah mengawal kos tersebut. Ia terbahagi\n"
"kepada tiga kumpulan:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Accuracy** options change the numerical value of the bounds, trading tightness for cost.\n"
msgstr "Pilihan **Ketepatan** mengubah nilai berangka sempadan, dengan menukar keketatan dengan kos.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Scope** determines *which* bounds are computed.\n"
msgstr "**Skop** menentukan sempadan *yang mana satu* dikira.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Execution** options change *how* the computation runs (not what it computes).\n"
msgstr "Pilihan **Pelaksanaan** mengubah *cara* pengiraan berjalan (bukan apa yang dikira).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Option | Default | Controls | Effect on the result |\n"
"| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n"
"| **Accuracy** | | | |\n"
"| `evolution_max_terms` | `1_000_000` | How many operator terms survive the evolution | Lower: cheaper, looser bounds |\n"
"| `atol_simplify` | `1e-8` | Which commutator terms are discarded as negligible | Higher: cheaper, looser bounds |\n"
"| `eigval_max_qubits` | `14` | How wide a commutator can be for its spectral norm to be computed | Lower: cheaper, looser bounds |\n"
"| `atol_eigenvalue` | `1e-10` | When the iterative eigensolver counts as converged | Higher: cheaper, less accurate bounds |\n"
"| **Scope** | | | |\n"
"| `max_num_boxes` | `None` | How many boxes have bounds computed | Boxes beyond the limit keep the trivial bound of 2.0 |\n"
"| **Execution** | | | |\n"
"| `timeout` | `None` | A wall-clock budget for the whole computation | Any remaining work keeps the trivial bound of 2.0 |\n"
"| `num_processes` | `1` | How many worker processes compute bounds in parallel | None on its own |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Pilihan | Lalai | Mengawal | Kesan pada hasil |\n"
"| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n"
"| **Ketepatan** | | | |\n"
"| `evolution_max_terms` | `1_000_000` | Berapa banyak sebutan operator yang kekal selepas evolusi | Lebih rendah: lebih murah, sempadan lebih longgar |\n"
"| `atol_simplify` | `1e-8` | Sebutan komutator yang mana dibuang sebagai boleh diabaikan | Lebih tinggi: lebih murah, sempadan lebih longgar |\n"
"| `eigval_max_qubits` | `14` | Selebar mana komutator boleh dikira norma spektrumnya | Lebih rendah: lebih murah, sempadan lebih longgar |\n"
"| `atol_eigenvalue` | `1e-10` | Bila penyelesai eigen lelaran dianggap telah menumpu | Lebih tinggi: lebih murah, sempadan kurang tepat |\n"
"| **Skop** | | | |\n"
"| `max_num_boxes` | `None` | Berapa banyak kotak yang sempadannya dikira | Kotak melebihi had mengekalkan sempadan remeh 2.0 |\n"
"| **Pelaksanaan** | | | |\n"
"| `timeout` | `None` | Bajet masa jam dinding untuk keseluruhan pengiraan | Sebarang kerja yang tinggal mengekalkan sempadan remeh 2.0 |\n"
"| `num_processes` | `1` | Berapa banyak proses pekerja mengira sempadan secara selari | Tiada kesan dengan sendirinya |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A bound is only useful if it is *valid*: it must never understate an error term's effect on the\n"
"observable. Loosening any of these options other than `atol_eigenvalue` can only make the bounds\n"
"larger (more conservative), never smaller. Thus, the cost of a loose setting is a larger sampling\n"
"overhead, not a wrong expectation value - [`atol_eigenvalue`](#atol_eigenvalue) is the exception.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sesuatu sempadan hanya berguna jika ia *sah*: ia tidak boleh sekali-kali memperkecilkan kesan sesuatu sebutan ralat terhadap\n"
"observabel. Melonggarkan mana-mana pilihan ini selain `atol_eigenvalue` hanya boleh menjadikan sempadan\n"
"lebih besar (lebih konservatif), tidak pernah lebih kecil. Oleh itu, kos tetapan yang longgar ialah overhed persampelan\n"
"yang lebih besar, bukan nilai jangkaan yang salah - [`atol_eigenvalue`](#atol_eigenvalue) ialah pengecualian.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Circuit definition {#circuit-definition}"
msgstr "Takrifan litar {#circuit-definition}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following experiments use the same Trotterized Ising circuit and observable as the [quickstart guide](/addons/qiskit-addon-slc/guides/quickstart). At\n"
"this size, every option has a visible effect while each computation still takes less than a second.\n"
msgstr ""
"Eksperimen berikut menggunakan litar Ising Trotter dan observabel yang sama seperti [panduan permulaan pantas](/addons/qiskit-addon-slc/guides/quickstart). Pada\n"
"saiz ini, setiap pilihan mempunyai kesan yang kelihatan manakala setiap pengiraan masih mengambil masa kurang daripada satu saat.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A small helper summarizes each set of bounds in one line, so the effect of an option shows up as a\n"
"few numbers rather than a wall of arrays.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pembantu kecil meringkaskan setiap set sempadan dalam satu baris, supaya kesan sesuatu pilihan muncul sebagai\n"
"beberapa nombor dan bukannya timbunan tatasusunan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Every bound lies between 0 and the trivial bound of 2.0. The summary reports the mean bound and its\n"
"standard deviation, followed by how the terms fall into these groups:\n"
"    - Terms bounded by exactly 0 because they commute with the evolved observable\n"
"    - Terms with a bound computed between 0 and 2.0\n"
"    - Terms left at the trivial 2.0\n"
msgstr ""
"Setiap sempadan terletak antara 0 dan sempadan remeh 2.0. Ringkasan melaporkan purata sempadan dan\n"
"sisihan piawainya, diikuti dengan cara sebutan terbahagi kepada kumpulan berikut:\n"
"    - Sebutan yang dibatasi tepat oleh 0 kerana ia mengkomut dengan observabel yang telah berevolusi\n"
"    - Sebutan dengan sempadan yang dikira antara 0 dan 2.0\n"
"    - Sebutan yang kekal pada 2.0 remeh\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note that **a lower mean is tighter, and tighter means a smaller sampling overhead later.**\n"
msgstr "Perhatikan bahawa **purata yang lebih rendah bermaksud lebih ketat, dan lebih ketat bermaksud overhed persampelan yang lebih kecil kemudian.**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A sweep over one option marks the option's default with `*`:\n"
msgstr "Sapuan ke atas satu pilihan menandakan lalai pilihan itu dengan `*`:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Accuracy {#accuracy}"
msgstr "Ketepatan {#accuracy}"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "`evolution_max_terms` {#evolution_max_terms}"
msgstr "`evolution_max_terms` {#evolution_max_terms}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Evolving a Pauli error term through non-Clifford gates turns it into a sum of Paulis, and that sum\n"
"grows with circuit depth. `evolution_max_terms` caps how many of those terms are kept. The 1-norm of\n"
"whatever is discarded is added to the bound, so nothing is silently lost.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mengembangkan sebutan ralat Pauli melalui get bukan Clifford menjadikannya hasil tambah Pauli, dan hasil tambah itu\n"
"bertambah besar dengan kedalaman litar. `evolution_max_terms` menghadkan berapa banyak sebutan itu disimpan. Norma-1\n"
"bagi apa sahaja yang dibuang ditambah kepada sempadan, jadi tiada apa yang hilang secara senyap.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The sweep runs from tighter than the default down to an extreme cut. Lowering the cap makes the\n"
"computation cheaper and the bounds looser.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sapuan bermula daripada lebih ketat berbanding lalai hingga ke pemotongan melampau. Menurunkan had menjadikan\n"
"pengiraan lebih murah dan sempadan lebih longgar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Raising the cap past its default changes nothing here. For a circuit of this size, the default\n"
"already keeps every term, so the bounds are as tight as this option can make them. That is the\n"
"typical situation. Tightening an accuracy option only pays off once its default is actually limiting,\n"
"and the way to find out is the experiment above. Rerun it with a tighter value and see whether the\n"
"bounds move.\n"
msgstr ""
"Menaikkan had melepasi lalainya tidak mengubah apa-apa di sini. Bagi litar bersaiz ini, lalai\n"
"sudah pun menyimpan setiap sebutan, jadi sempadan adalah seketat yang boleh dicapai oleh pilihan ini. Itulah\n"
"situasi lazim. Mengetatkan pilihan ketepatan hanya berbaloi apabila lalainya benar-benar menghad,\n"
"dan cara untuk mengetahuinya ialah eksperimen di atas. Jalankan semula dengan nilai yang lebih ketat dan lihat sama ada\n"
"sempadan bergerak.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<div class=\"alert alert-warning\">\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Warning:** The underlying propagation routine treats `evolution_max_terms` as a *capacity to\n"
"pre-allocate*, not as an upper limit to check against. Passing something nominally unlimited, such\n"
"as `numpy.iinfo(numpy.uint).max`, asks the allocator for terabytes of memory and aborts the process.\n"
"Keep it to a realistic number. The default of one million is already generous.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Amaran:** Rutin perambatan asas menganggap `evolution_max_terms` sebagai *kapasiti untuk\n"
"pra-peruntukan*, bukan sebagai had atas untuk disemak. Memasukkan sesuatu yang kononnya tanpa had, seperti\n"
"`numpy.iinfo(numpy.uint).max`, meminta pengagih memori sebanyak terabait dan menghentikan proses.\n"
"Kekalkan pada nombor yang realistik. Lalai satu juta sudah memadai.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "</div>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "`atol_simplify` {#atol_simplify}"
msgstr "`atol_simplify` {#atol_simplify}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"After the commutator is formed, terms with a coefficient below `atol_simplify` are dropped. As with\n"
"the evolution cap, the 1-norm lost this way is added to the bound.\n"
msgstr ""
"Selepas komutator dibentuk, sebutan dengan pekali di bawah `atol_simplify` dibuang. Seperti\n"
"had evolusi, norma-1 yang hilang dengan cara ini ditambah kepada sempadan.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "`eigval_max_qubits` {#eigval_max_qubits}"
msgstr "`eigval_max_qubits` {#eigval_max_qubits}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The tightest available bound is the spectral norm of the commutator, which needs an eigenvalue\n"
"computation. That becomes expensive as the commutator widens, so `eigval_max_qubits` sets the width\n"
"beyond which the attempt is abandoned in favour of the triangle inequality. That bound,\n"
"$2 \\sum_i |c_i|$ over the commutator's coefficients $c_i$, is valid but looser.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sempadan paling ketat yang tersedia ialah norma spektrum komutator, yang memerlukan pengiraan\n"
"nilai eigen. Itu menjadi mahal apabila komutator melebar, jadi `eigval_max_qubits` menetapkan lebar\n"
"melebihi yang mana percubaan ditinggalkan dan digantikan dengan ketaksamaan segi tiga. Sempadan itu,\n"
"$2 \\sum_i |c_i|$ ke atas pekali komutator $c_i$, adalah sah tetapi lebih longgar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Setting it to zero forces the fallback everywhere, which shows the benefit of the eigensolver\n"
"in one number.\n"
msgstr ""
"Menetapkannya kepada sifar memaksa penggunaan alternatif di mana-mana, yang menunjukkan manfaat penyelesai eigen\n"
"dalam satu nombor.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Even with the eigensolver switched off, the mean stays far below the trivial 2.0. The share\n"
"of terms bounded by 0 does not change: a term that commutes exactly with the evolved observable\n"
"has a zero commutator, which is recognized before any eigenvalue computation is considered. Of the\n"
"others, the triangle-inequality bound reaches 2.0 for some and is capped there, but for many it is\n"
"still smaller, so they keep a computed bound below 2.0.\n"
msgstr ""
"Walaupun penyelesai eigen dimatikan, purata kekal jauh di bawah 2.0 remeh. Bahagian\n"
"sebutan yang dibatasi oleh 0 tidak berubah: sebutan yang mengkomut tepat dengan observabel yang telah berevolusi\n"
"mempunyai komutator sifar, yang dikenali sebelum sebarang pengiraan nilai eigen dipertimbangkan. Bagi\n"
"yang lain, sempadan ketaksamaan segi tiga mencapai 2.0 untuk sesetengahnya dan dihadkan di situ, tetapi bagi banyak yang lain\n"
"ia masih lebih kecil, jadi ia mengekalkan sempadan yang dikira di bawah 2.0.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "`atol_eigenvalue` {#atol_eigenvalue}"
msgstr "`atol_eigenvalue` {#atol_eigenvalue}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When the spectral norm *is* computed, `atol_eigenvalue` is the convergence tolerance of the\n"
"iterative eigensolver. Most commutators never reach that solver, though:\n"
msgstr ""
"Apabila norma spektrum *dikira*, `atol_eigenvalue` ialah toleransi penumpuan bagi\n"
"penyelesai eigen lelaran. Walau bagaimanapun, kebanyakan komutator tidak pernah sampai kepada penyelesai itu:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A commutator acting on at most four qubits is diagonalized exactly, directly.\n"
msgstr "Komutator yang bertindak pada paling banyak empat qubit didiagonalkan secara tepat, terus.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A wider one is first reduced to the smallest number of qubits that its Pauli terms need,\n"
"and if that reduced form acts on at most eight qubits, it is diagonalized exactly.\n"
msgstr ""
"Komutator yang lebih lebar mula-mula dikurangkan kepada bilangan qubit terkecil yang diperlukan oleh sebutan Paulinya,\n"
"dan jika bentuk terkurang itu bertindak pada paling banyak lapan qubit, ia didiagonalkan secara tepat.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Only a commutator that still needs more than eight qubits after that reduction goes to the iterative\n"
"solver, which is the only place this tolerance applies. Circuits of the size used in this guide never get\n"
"that far, so a sweep over this option would show identical bounds for every value. It matters for\n"
"wide light cones on large devices.\n"
msgstr ""
"Hanya komutator yang masih memerlukan lebih daripada lapan qubit selepas pengurangan itu pergi kepada penyelesai\n"
"lelaran, iaitu satu-satunya tempat toleransi ini terpakai. Litar bersaiz seperti yang digunakan dalam panduan ini tidak pernah\n"
"sampai sejauh itu, jadi sapuan ke atas pilihan ini akan menunjukkan sempadan yang sama bagi setiap nilai. Ia penting untuk\n"
"kon cahaya yang lebar pada peranti besar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Unlike the other accuracy options, loosening `atol_eigenvalue` is *not* safe in one direction. An\n"
"iterative eigensolver approaches the extremal eigenvalue from inside the spectrum, so an estimate\n"
"that has not fully converged understates the spectral norm, and the bound. The default is\n"
"deliberately tight for that reason. If the solver fails to converge, the triangle-inequality\n"
"fallback takes over, which is valid again.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tidak seperti pilihan ketepatan yang lain, melonggarkan `atol_eigenvalue` *tidak* selamat dalam satu arah. Penyelesai eigen\n"
"lelaran menghampiri nilai eigen ekstrem dari dalam spektrum, jadi anggaran\n"
"yang belum menumpu sepenuhnya memperkecilkan norma spektrum, dan juga sempadan. Lalai\n"
"disengajakan ketat atas sebab itu. Jika penyelesai gagal menumpu, alternatif ketaksamaan\n"
"segi tiga mengambil alih, yang sah semula.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Scope {#scope}"
msgstr "Skop {#scope}"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "`max_num_boxes` {#max_num_boxes}"
msgstr "`max_num_boxes` {#max_num_boxes}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Sometimes the useful limit is not accuracy but depth. `max_num_boxes` stops spawning bound\n"
"computations past a given number of boxes, and every layer beyond it is assigned the trivial bound\n"
"of 2.0 instead.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kadangkala had yang berguna bukan ketepatan tetapi kedalaman. `max_num_boxes` berhenti menjana pengiraan\n"
"sempadan melepasi bilangan kotak tertentu, dan setiap lapisan di luarnya diberikan sempadan remeh\n"
"2.0 sebagai ganti.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The limit counts the noisy `BoxOp` instructions (those carrying an `InjectNoise` annotation) rather\n"
"than, for example, a depth in gates. That keeps it tied to the user-visible structure of the circuit and\n"
"avoids coupling to the auto-generated annotation references, which can change between\n"
"transpilation runs.\n"
msgstr ""
"Had itu mengira arahan `BoxOp` yang bising (yang membawa anotasi `InjectNoise`) dan bukannya,\n"
"sebagai contoh, kedalaman dalam get. Itu mengekalkannya terikat kepada struktur litar yang kelihatan oleh pengguna dan\n"
"mengelakkan gandingan dengan rujukan anotasi yang dijana secara automatik, yang boleh berubah antara\n"
"jalankan transpilasi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is the natural choice for a circuit whose two halves are handled by forward and backward bounds\n"
"respectively: compute each only as deep as it will be used.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini pilihan semula jadi bagi litar yang dua separuhnya dikendalikan oleh sempadan hadapan dan belakang\n"
"masing-masing: kira setiap satu hanya sedalam yang akan digunakan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Execution {#execution}"
msgstr "Pelaksanaan {#execution}"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "`timeout` {#timeout}"
msgstr "`timeout` {#timeout}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`timeout` is a wall-clock budget in seconds. When it expires, the bounds that have been computed are kept\n"
"and everything outstanding keeps the trivial bound of 2.0, so the result is always usable, just\n"
"looser the earlier you cut it off.\n"
msgstr ""
"`timeout` ialah bajet masa jam dinding dalam saat. Apabila ia tamat, sempadan yang telah dikira dikekalkan\n"
"dan semua yang belum selesai mengekalkan sempadan remeh 2.0, jadi hasilnya sentiasa boleh digunakan, cuma\n"
"lebih longgar jika dihentikan lebih awal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It is not a hard deadline: already-running tasks are allowed to finish, so the call can overrun the\n"
"budget by the duration of one task.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ia bukan tarikh akhir yang tegar: tugas yang sedang berjalan dibenarkan untuk selesai, jadi panggilan boleh melebihi\n"
"bajet sebanyak tempoh satu tugas.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "`num_processes` {#num_processes}"
msgstr "`num_processes` {#num_processes}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Bounds for different error terms are independent, so `num_processes` distributes them over worker\n"
"processes. On its own, this affects only how long the computation takes, never its result.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sempadan bagi sebutan ralat yang berbeza adalah bebas, jadi `num_processes` mengagihkannya ke atas proses\n"
"pekerja. Dengan sendirinya, ini hanya menjejaskan berapa lama pengiraan mengambil masa, tidak pernah hasilnya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<div class=\"alert alert-info\">\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Note:** A `timeout` combined with `num_processes` makes the result depend on timing: which tasks\n"
"finish before the budget expires is not deterministic. The bounds stay valid, but they are no longer\n"
"reproducible from run to run.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Nota:** `timeout` yang digabungkan dengan `num_processes` menjadikan hasil bergantung pada masa: tugas mana yang\n"
"selesai sebelum bajet tamat tidak deterministik. Sempadan kekal sah, tetapi ia tidak lagi\n"
"boleh dihasilkan semula dari satu larian ke larian yang lain.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Where to start {#where-to-start}"
msgstr "Di mana hendak bermula {#where-to-start}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The defaults are chosen to give tight bounds on circuits of a size where that is affordable. When a\n"
"computation is too slow, try applying the options in roughly this order:\n"
msgstr ""
"Lalai dipilih untuk memberikan sempadan yang ketat pada litar bersaiz yang mampu ditanggung. Apabila\n"
"pengiraan terlalu perlahan, cuba gunakan pilihan mengikut urutan kasar ini:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`num_processes`: A free speed-up, with no accuracy cost.\n"
msgstr "`num_processes`: Peningkatan kelajuan percuma, tanpa kos ketepatan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`max_num_boxes`: If you know in advance how deep into the circuit you care about.\n"
msgstr "`max_num_boxes`: Jika anda tahu lebih awal sedalam mana dalam litar yang anda ambil kisah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`eigval_max_qubits`: Skips the most expensive step for the widest commutators, which are usually\n"
"a small minority of the terms.\n"
msgstr ""
"`eigval_max_qubits`: Melangkau langkah paling mahal bagi komutator terlebar, yang biasanya\n"
"segelintir kecil daripada sebutan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`evolution_max_terms` and `atol_simplify`: These impact accuracy throughout, so tune\n"
"them last, checking with a sweep like the ones above to determine how far the bounds move.\n"
msgstr ""
"`evolution_max_terms` dan `atol_simplify`: Ini menjejaskan ketepatan secara menyeluruh, jadi laraskan\n"
"yang terakhir, sambil menyemak dengan sapuan seperti yang di atas untuk menentukan sejauh mana sempadan bergerak.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`timeout`: A hard stop rather than a tuning aid, for when a computation must finish by a deadline,\n"
"whatever the quality.\n"
msgstr ""
"`timeout`: Penghentian tegar dan bukan bantuan penalaan, untuk ketika pengiraan mesti selesai menjelang tarikh akhir,\n"
"walau apa pun kualitinya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The looser the bounds, the larger the sampling overhead that `compute_local_scales` will report for\n"
"a given bias tolerance. That overhead is the quantity worth watching while tuning: it tells you what\n"
"the approximations actually cost.\n"
msgstr ""
"Semakin longgar sempadan, semakin besar overhed persampelan yang akan dilaporkan oleh `compute_local_scales` bagi\n"
"toleransi pincang tertentu. Overhed itu ialah kuantiti yang patut dipantau semasa penalaan: ia memberitahu anda apa\n"
"kos sebenar hampiran tersebut.\n"
